{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612803-cloak-of-the-night-during-fight","id":612803,"title":"cloak of the night during fight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-02T17:25:19-07:00","id":612803,"title":"cloak of the night during fight","content":"The corebook 2'nd ed says that isn't required any dice roll to disappear, even in front of someone, using cloak of the night. But my question is: if the vamp try to vanish during a fight against another vampire or a werewolf?? Is this automatically happens? Aren't there any contested rolls? If the vampire have auspex for example? And with what gift could a werewolf see or attack a vanished vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:52:52-07:00","id":612855,"title":"","content":"No, there's no contested roll. You need to either take the vampire out before he can get the instant action off, or have access to Auspex or a similar sensory power to provoke a clash of wills and win. Werewolves do have access to at least one gift (and I don't remember its name) that can provoke a clash of wills on obfuscate, as will probably every other splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7080-armadeo","name":"Armadeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:55:26-07:00","id":612859,"title":"","content":"As written, nothing stops the power from working, no strings attached. Use of Auspex can pierce Obfuscate on a won Clash Of Wills roll, and other powers that reveal supernatural concealment may likewise be able to pierce it by winning on a Clash Of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:34:40-07:00","id":612879,"title":"","content":"Ok thank you. But now I have another question. If the vampire haven't auspex or the werewolf haven't an appropriate gift, a vampire with obfuscation could, during a fight: use obfuscation, attack behind the shoulder (so deny the defense) , face the attack from enemy, using obfuscate again and repeat the surprise attack. Isn't this use of obfuscate too strong ? Is there anything I'm doing wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-02-2015, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T18:52:56-07:00","id":612892,"title":"","content":"Attacking behind the shoulder will use up his instant action for the round. He won't be able to dodge or put up Cloak of the Night until the next turn, leaving him open for attack each round he does it. Furthermore, Cloak of the Night does use up one vitae each time he uses it. Constantly dropping it and reactivating it will run him out of vitae eventually.<br /> <br /> All-in-all it's strong, but far from overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7080-armadeo","name":"Armadeo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T23:54:27-07:00","id":613059,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that doing it to a Werewolf will likely start pissing them off really badly and they may well go into their killing form and then just auto heal all the damage you deal each time you sneak attack until you run out of blood and then they eat your head. Or you run away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T01:47:54-07:00","id":613090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612803-cloak-of-the-night-during-fight?p=613059#post613059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bear in mind that doing it to a Werewolf will likely start pissing them off really badly and they may well go into their killing form and then just auto heal all the damage you deal each time you sneak attack until you run out of blood and then they eat your head. Or you run away.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes unless I use aggravated damage :P<br /> Anyway it was just a general question to understand better this mechanics <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:41:44-07:00","id":613115,"title":"","content":"Wait a second: i thought you could use Obfuscate 3 now when in combat, even if you strike someone while obfuscated. I mean, now you can simply activate the power and fight, without having to reactivate it or losing it when fighting, am i wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:45:28-07:00","id":613120,"title":"","content":"It doesn't drop when in combat, but if you attack someone then they get to see you. You can obfuscate yourself and your target to have a death match in front of a crowd and nobody would know, until you start messing up the furniture, but the combat would be normal as you and your opponent could see each other (after the first strike).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T02:58:55-07:00","id":613154,"title":"","content":"@Phersus: You lose you invisibility against whoever you just attacked. If you want to make another surprise attack on the same person, you need to reactivate it.<br /> <br /> @Marcus: Also note that attacking someone while obfuscated gives you a bonus to your roll to surprise them, it doesn't let you automatically succeed.<br /> <br /> For even more surprise attacks, use Celerity's third active effect. It's reflexive!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T03:07:45-07:00","id":613157,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for your answers mates! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T10:29:41-07:00","id":613623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/612803-cloak-of-the-night-during-fight?p=613154#post613154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For even more surprise attacks, use Celerity's third active effect. It's reflexive!</div> </div> </div> </div>Activating it is reflexive, but making an attack is still instant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}